From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 05 May 2026 15:22:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: nft_flow_offload: add DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA direct xmit path

Without a DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA case, the default switch arm NULLs
info->indev and SW flow offload silently fails for eth-to-wifi bridged
flows. Handle the path type by populating indev/outdev, recording the
source MAC, and selecting FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_DIRECT so packets bypass
bridge and route lookups once conntrack establishes the flow.

Pairs with the mt76 patch that fills DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA when WED is
disabled.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 net/netfilter/nft_flow_offload.c |    8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/net/netfilter/nft_flow_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nft_flow_offload.c
@@ -160,6 +160,14 @@ static void nft_dev_path_info(const stru
 			}
 			info->xmit_type = FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_DIRECT;
 			break;
+		case DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA:
+			info->indev = path->dev;
+			if (!info->outdev)
+				info->outdev = path->dev;
+			if (is_zero_ether_addr(info->h_source))
+				memcpy(info->h_source, path->dev->dev_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+			info->xmit_type = FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_DIRECT;
+			break;
 		default:
 			info->indev = NULL;
 			break;
